WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.001 --> 00:00:03.069
-The House impeachment managers

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:04.570
have presented a damning
and powerful case

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:06.072
against former president
Donald Trump this week,

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:08.240
including harrowing new scenes
of violence

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.810
from the Capitol riot and never-
before-seen security footage

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:12.711
of lawmakers being rushed away
from the mob.

00:00:12.711 --> 00:00:15.715
The evidence makes clear that
the attack was much worse

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:19.051
than we knew, that it could have
been even worse than it was,

00:00:19.051 --> 00:00:21.554
and that it was directed
explicitly by Trump,

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:23.890
and yet Republicans have made
clear they just don't care.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:26.559
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:30.563
♪♪

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:32.899
The thing about Donald Trump
is that it's always clear

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:35.835
exactly who he has been
since day one of his campaign.

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:37.203
There was no confusion.

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:39.205
It's like when the great
Michael Shannon

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:40.373
pops up in a movie,

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:42.175
you immediately know
he's the bad guy.

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:44.344
Michael Shannon's not there
to rescue puppies

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:46.513
or provide sage advice
to newlyweds.

00:00:46.513 --> 00:00:49.615
He's there to steal his father's
inheritance or kill Superman.

00:00:49.615 --> 00:00:51.951
Or maybe he's starring
in a Ted Cruz biopic.

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:53.119
It's hard to tell.

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:56.790
Anyway, everyone knew
what Trump was about

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.624
and what his movement was about.

00:00:58.624 --> 00:01:01.293
He tapped into something ugly
and horrifying

00:01:01.293 --> 00:01:03.296
at the heart of the modern
Republican Party,

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:04.764
and the threat
of political violence

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:06.232
played a central role in that.

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:08.868
He repeatedly encouraged his
supporters to physically attack

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:11.971
protesters and promised to pay
their legal bills,

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:13.973
which we know now,
of course, was a lie.

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:15.975
I mean, he can't even pay
his own legal bills.

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:18.644
He stiffed Rudy, the one lawyer
who was willing to defend Trump

00:01:18.644 --> 00:01:20.880
by flying cross-country
and lying about the election,

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.049
finding witnesses
outside package stores,

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:24.884
and holding press conferences

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:27.219
and also, I'm guessing, sleeping

00:01:27.219 --> 00:01:28.554
at landscaping companies.

00:01:28.554 --> 00:01:29.889
[ As Giuliani ]
Oh, no need for a cot.

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:31.390
I'll just curl up in the mulch!

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:33.392
[ Normal voice ] Plus,
forget paying for them --

00:01:33.392 --> 00:01:34.894
based on his lawyers,

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:37.397
would you really want
Donald Trump picking yours?

00:01:37.397 --> 00:01:39.465
I'm starting to think
he buys his in bulk

00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:42.468
at Bob's Partially Damaged
Lawyers Discount Basement.

00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:44.070
"This one's good
on the Constitution,

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:46.739
but he craps himself every time
he hears the word 'objection.'"

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:49.375
"Can I get that one
in a suit that fits?"

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:51.210
"No, everything here is as is."

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:52.545
"Can I get that one

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:54.513
with a briefcase
instead of a grocery bag?"

00:01:54.513 --> 00:01:56.483
"As is!"

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:59.819
And not only has it been clear
who Trump was from day one,

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:02.321
but the people who publicly
warned us about him

00:02:02.321 --> 00:02:04.023
are now his strongest
supporters.

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:06.525
-Presidents can't just say
whatever they want.

00:02:06.525 --> 00:02:08.694
There are consequences
to the words of a president.

00:02:08.694 --> 00:02:10.196
There are consequences
to the words

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:12.031
of a presidential candidate,
as well.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.699
You have a candidate
in Donald Trump

00:02:13.699 --> 00:02:17.002
who clearly has used language
that appeals to anger

00:02:17.002 --> 00:02:19.672
and in some instances has
actually said to the crowd,

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:21.173
"No, let's beat this person up"

00:02:21.173 --> 00:02:22.942
and let's do this
or let's do that.

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:24.944
So it shouldn't surprise us that
you see a growing amount

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:26.445
of violence
at some of his events.

00:02:26.445 --> 00:02:28.113
There's only one
presidential candidate

00:02:28.113 --> 00:02:29.448
who has violence
at their events.

00:02:29.448 --> 00:02:31.250
-Ooh, ooh, wait, wait!
Can I guess who it is?

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.786
Uh...I don't think
it's John Kasich,

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:35.955
unless he was bullying
his supporters into

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:37.624
signing up with TD Ameritrade.

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:39.124
Certainly, it couldn't
have been Bernie.

00:02:39.124 --> 00:02:41.161
I'm guessing the closest
Bernie comes to violence

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:43.563
is using a firm tone when
somebody mixes up

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:46.732
the Bosc and Bartlett pears
at the Burlington food co-op.

00:02:46.732 --> 00:02:47.901
[ As Sanders ]
You have to keep them separate.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:50.069
One is crisp
and the other is sweet.

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:52.238
If I see you mixing them up
again, I'll have no choice

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:55.073
but to gently clap your ears
with my adorable mittens.

00:02:55.073 --> 00:02:57.744
[ Normal voice ] In fact, this
is the most violent thing

00:02:57.744 --> 00:02:59.645
I believe Bernie has ever said
in his life.

00:02:59.645 --> 00:03:03.983
-You know, I eat extra sharp.
That's what I eat.

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:05.984
You know, they produce
great cheese

00:03:05.984 --> 00:03:08.654
and they're internationally
known for what they do.

00:03:08.654 --> 00:03:10.656
-That's right, Bernie's cheese
is extra sharp,

00:03:10.656 --> 00:03:12.425
just like his tongue.

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:14.927
Anyway, Marco Rubio predicted
this five years ago.

00:03:14.927 --> 00:03:18.597
In fact, his vision of what
a Trump presidency would be like

00:03:18.597 --> 00:03:20.033
was eerily accurate.

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:21.701
-The great thing about
our Republic is that

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:24.537
we settle our differences in
this country at the ballot box,

00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:27.206
not with guns or
bayonets or violence.

00:03:27.206 --> 00:03:29.208
And you wonder whether we're
headed in a different direction

00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:32.045
today, where we're no longer
able or capable of having

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:34.213
differences of opinion,
but in fact,

00:03:34.213 --> 00:03:36.682
now protests become a license
to take violence,

00:03:36.682 --> 00:03:39.652
to take on your opponents
physically.

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:43.322
This is what happens when
a leading presidential candidate

00:03:43.322 --> 00:03:45.991
goes around feeding into
a narrative of anger

00:03:45.991 --> 00:03:47.860
and bitterness and frustration,

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:50.730
and I think we all need to take
a step back and ask ourselves,

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.565
are we contributing to this?

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:54.233
-Well, did you ask yourself?

00:03:54.233 --> 00:03:57.236
Or are you still taking
steps back five years later,

00:03:57.236 --> 00:04:01.573
which would put you almost
into international waters?

00:04:01.573 --> 00:04:04.076
So, that was Rubio
all the way back in 2016 --

00:04:04.076 --> 00:04:05.911
you know, back when he went by
"Little Marco."

00:04:05.911 --> 00:04:07.413
He's all grown up now!

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:09.949
But in that clip,
Marco is basically laying out

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:12.118
the same argument
Democrats are making today.

00:04:12.118 --> 00:04:13.619
In fact, he's passionate
about it.

00:04:13.619 --> 00:04:16.122
And yet despite there being
more evidence

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:18.958
that Rubio was right then,
he and his gang

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:21.628
have instead actively chosen
to collude with evil

00:04:21.628 --> 00:04:23.862
and abandon whatever they may
have believed about Donald Trump

00:04:23.862 --> 00:04:25.531
five years ago
in order to advance

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:27.700
their political careers
and obtain power.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:30.803
Which is how -- fast-forward
five years -- you get this.

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:32.404
-This impeachment trial,
let me ask you,

00:04:32.404 --> 00:04:34.473
how many people are gonna get
vaccinated because of this

00:04:34.473 --> 00:04:36.376
impeachment trial?
None.

00:04:36.376 --> 00:04:37.876
How many people
are gonna find a job

00:04:37.876 --> 00:04:39.212
because of this
impeachment trial?

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:40.280
None.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:41.614
How many people
are gonna be helped

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:43.282
to put their kids back in school

00:04:43.282 --> 00:04:44.617
because of this
impeachment trial?

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:45.885
None.

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:48.053
We are going to spend a week
focused on something

00:04:48.053 --> 00:04:50.756
that is not going to help anyone
with the thing that matters

00:04:50.756 --> 00:04:53.425
in this country the most
right now.

00:04:53.425 --> 00:04:56.562
And that's a terrible thing.
That's a waste of our time.

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:58.864
-Ask yourself, how many people
are gonna get superpowers

00:04:58.864 --> 00:05:00.533
from this impeachment trial?
None.

00:05:00.533 --> 00:05:02.334
How many people are gonna
fall in love because of this

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:03.836
impeachment trial?
None.

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:05.838
How many people are gonna win
the McDonald's Monopoly

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:08.240
million-dollar grand prize
by collecting all four railroads

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:10.242
from containers of large
or medium-size fries

00:05:10.242 --> 00:05:12.077
or McFlurries or apple pies?
None.

00:05:12.077 --> 00:05:15.081
Because you can't get the
railroads from the apple pies,

00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:17.784
even though they're one of
the most popular menu items.

00:05:17.784 --> 00:05:20.687
You have to buy the McNuggets,
the Big Mac or the Filet-O-Fish,

00:05:20.687 --> 00:05:23.021
even though no one wants the
Filet-O-Fish because it tastes

00:05:23.021 --> 00:05:24.356
like deep-fried cat food.

00:05:24.356 --> 00:05:26.158
And God forbid
you leave a Filet-O-Fish

00:05:26.158 --> 00:05:28.160
in your car overnight --
that's it for that car.

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:30.229
Nobody will even tow it for you.
What I'm saying is,

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:32.131
Impeachment is a waste of time.

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:34.400
But that's not
what impeachment is for.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:37.569
You should be capable of doing
two or three

00:05:37.569 --> 00:05:40.039
or even, God forbid,
four things at once.

00:05:40.039 --> 00:05:42.541
If you really want to help
people out,

00:05:42.541 --> 00:05:45.377
why not sign on to
the Democrats' COVID relief bill

00:05:45.377 --> 00:05:47.212
or a $15 minimum wage?

00:05:47.212 --> 00:05:49.948
If you care so much about the
pandemic or poverty

00:05:49.948 --> 00:05:52.150
or child hunger, where were you

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:54.487
when the previous president
was shoveling trillions

00:05:54.487 --> 00:05:56.656
into the pockets of rich people
and corporations

00:05:56.656 --> 00:05:59.458
and telling everyone COVID would
magically disappear

00:05:59.458 --> 00:06:02.228
so long as they stick a few
Tide to Go pens up their noses?

00:06:02.228 --> 00:06:03.629
Why didn't you say anything?

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:04.797
Why did you spend four years

00:06:04.797 --> 00:06:06.632
cryptically tweeting
Bible quotes

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:08.133
like some kind of serial killer

00:06:08.133 --> 00:06:10.136
or a Southern
chicken restaurant?

00:06:10.136 --> 00:06:14.240
Because you're a boneless fraud
who dresses less like a senator

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:16.575
and more like an assistant
high school basketball coach

00:06:16.575 --> 00:06:18.577
who gets fired for stealing
towels from the locker room.

00:06:18.577 --> 00:06:21.013
Seriously, dude,
did you win that hat

00:06:21.013 --> 00:06:23.916
in a local radio station contest
by calling in and guessing

00:06:23.916 --> 00:06:25.818
the number-one hit
in March 1995?

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:27.319
You look like you got
your entire outfit

00:06:27.319 --> 00:06:30.723
from a T-shirt cannon fired by
the Phoenix Suns gorilla.

00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:32.892
Also, does your hat
match your chair?

00:06:32.892 --> 00:06:35.228
Because that's weird.
Don't do that.

00:06:35.228 --> 00:06:37.729
And then this morning,
a grown-up Marco decided

00:06:37.729 --> 00:06:39.899
to wear a big-boy suit,
go on "Fox &amp; Friends,"

00:06:39.899 --> 00:06:41.567
and once again dismiss
the trial,

00:06:41.567 --> 00:06:42.935
the harrowing scenes of violence

00:06:42.935 --> 00:06:44.703
and the never-before-seen
security footage

00:06:44.703 --> 00:06:46.204
as a waste of time.

00:06:46.204 --> 00:06:48.874
-They spent a lot of time
yesterday convincing us

00:06:48.874 --> 00:06:50.843
of what I already knew
and believed, and that is

00:06:50.843 --> 00:06:52.678
that the attack on January 6th

00:06:52.678 --> 00:06:56.515
was outrageous,
criminal, deadly.

00:06:56.515 --> 00:06:59.418
It could have been far worse.
I knew that, as well.

00:06:59.418 --> 00:07:01.587
So I don't think there's any
dispute about that.

00:07:01.587 --> 00:07:04.190
The question is whether
impeachment, which is designed

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:07.026
clearly to remove someone from
office, is the appropriate thing

00:07:07.026 --> 00:07:08.861
to do when someone
is no longer in office.

00:07:08.861 --> 00:07:10.696
And my answer to that is no.

00:07:10.696 --> 00:07:12.498
-Oh, man, if only
current Marco Rubio

00:07:12.498 --> 00:07:14.332
could meet 2016 Marco Rubio.

00:07:14.332 --> 00:07:17.169
It would be like a sci-fi movie
where you have to choose

00:07:17.169 --> 00:07:19.571
between two clones,
except they both suck

00:07:19.571 --> 00:07:21.139
because they in turn are clones

00:07:21.139 --> 00:07:23.810
of the third clone
who also sucked.

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:26.645
Also, that's not actually what
impeachment is designed for.

00:07:26.645 --> 00:07:28.314
The framers were clear
about this.

00:07:28.314 --> 00:07:30.816
The Constitution explicitly
gives the Senate the power

00:07:30.816 --> 00:07:33.151
to bar someone from ever holding
public office again.

00:07:33.151 --> 00:07:35.087
In fact, as we speak,

00:07:35.087 --> 00:07:37.423
Trump is also under criminal
investigation in Georgia

00:07:37.423 --> 00:07:39.058
for trying to steal
the election.

00:07:39.058 --> 00:07:41.393
And if you ask me, inciting
a violent, seditious mob

00:07:41.393 --> 00:07:44.230
to storm the Capitol where they
went after the vice president,

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:46.232
the speaker of the house,
and members of Congress,

00:07:46.232 --> 00:07:48.434
and where they injured
140 police officers

00:07:48.434 --> 00:07:51.770
sounds like pretty good reason
to be barred from public office.

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:53.772
I mean, you can get barred
from Hooters

00:07:53.772 --> 00:07:55.774
for not wearing a shirt
and shoes.

00:07:55.774 --> 00:07:57.610
Place is named after
bare breasts,

00:07:57.610 --> 00:07:59.945
and you still have to
wear a shirt.

00:07:59.945 --> 00:08:01.780
We've all seen the damning
video footage this week.

00:08:01.780 --> 00:08:03.115
It's haunting.

00:08:03.115 --> 00:08:05.117
And yet the Republican Party
and its media apparatus

00:08:05.117 --> 00:08:07.419
aren't just looking
the other way metaphorically --

00:08:07.419 --> 00:08:09.421
they're looking away literally.

00:08:09.421 --> 00:08:12.024
Rubio, along with a few other
GOP senators,

00:08:12.024 --> 00:08:14.126
reportedly looked down
at some papers

00:08:14.126 --> 00:08:15.962
as the harrowing footage played.

00:08:15.962 --> 00:08:17.963
There was also previously unseen
camera footage

00:08:17.963 --> 00:08:20.633
of vice President Mike Pence
and Senator Mitt Romney

00:08:20.633 --> 00:08:22.501
being rushed away
from the mob to safety.

00:08:22.501 --> 00:08:25.905
We learned that House Speaker
Nancy Pelosi had to be evacuated

00:08:25.905 --> 00:08:28.907
from the entire Capitol complex
for her safety.

00:08:28.907 --> 00:08:30.643
At least show some concern

00:08:30.643 --> 00:08:32.311
for the physical safety
of your colleagues.

00:08:32.311 --> 00:08:35.547
If someone showed me a hostage
video of my friend Fred Armisen

00:08:35.547 --> 00:08:37.416
waving to get my attention
because he was being

00:08:37.416 --> 00:08:39.585
held captive in a room
by kidnappers,

00:08:39.585 --> 00:08:41.888
I wouldn't just ignore it
and move on.

00:08:44.757 --> 00:08:46.192
Uh, not now, Fred.

00:08:46.192 --> 00:08:48.193
And then there's Missouri
Senator Josh Hawley,

00:08:48.193 --> 00:08:51.497
the guy who got kicked out of
Cobra Kai for being too slimy

00:08:51.497 --> 00:08:53.165
and then wrote an op-ed titled

00:08:53.165 --> 00:08:55.333
"How I Got Cobra Kaincelled."

00:08:55.333 --> 00:08:57.503
Hawley not only ignored
the harrowing video footage,

00:08:57.503 --> 00:08:59.338
but made himself comfortable
while doing it.

00:08:59.338 --> 00:09:02.508
-Josh Hawley, who's made his
disdain for this process

00:09:02.508 --> 00:09:04.543
abundantly clear
in public comments,

00:09:04.543 --> 00:09:06.245
was doing the same
thing in the chamber.

00:09:06.245 --> 00:09:08.580
All of the senators have
the option to use the gallery,

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:11.917
the upstairs area for seating
for social distancing.

00:09:11.917 --> 00:09:13.752
Josh Hawley is the only one
taking advantage

00:09:13.752 --> 00:09:15.421
of that opportunity.
He's been sitting

00:09:15.421 --> 00:09:18.090
with his legs up on the seat
in front of him

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:20.559
essentially reading
non-related material.

00:09:20.559 --> 00:09:22.061
-Of course he was.

00:09:22.061 --> 00:09:24.062
Hawley is the richest kid
in high school

00:09:24.062 --> 00:09:27.332
who during the memorial assembly
for the beloved librarian

00:09:27.332 --> 00:09:30.369
loudly comments on the "Playboy"
hidden in his science book.

00:09:30.369 --> 00:09:32.905
"We will all miss
Debra's love of reading."

00:09:32.905 --> 00:09:36.241
"Yowza, Joshy like!"

00:09:36.241 --> 00:09:38.644
And then there was Fox News,
which actually had the gall

00:09:38.644 --> 00:09:39.978
to cut away from the trial

00:09:39.978 --> 00:09:41.981
in the middle
of the harrowing testimony

00:09:41.981 --> 00:09:44.817
to get to Jesse Watters
and Jeanine Pirro.

00:09:44.817 --> 00:09:48.821
-You may have heard one man
yelled, "No violence,"

00:09:48.821 --> 00:09:52.624
and another responded,
"It's too late for that."

00:09:52.624 --> 00:09:56.295
♪♪

00:09:56.295 --> 00:09:57.729
-Hello, everybody,
I'm Jesse Watters,

00:09:57.729 --> 00:10:00.465
along with Juan Williams,
Dana Perino,

00:10:00.465 --> 00:10:02.968
Greg Gutfeld,
and Judge Jeanine Pirro.

00:10:02.968 --> 00:10:04.636
-That's right, they cut off
the impeachment trial.

00:10:04.636 --> 00:10:06.571
Usually, these two are the ones
getting cut off.

00:10:06.571 --> 00:10:08.641
At any time,
you could ask Jesse Watters

00:10:08.641 --> 00:10:10.743
to blow into a breathalyzer
and the result would probably

00:10:10.743 --> 00:10:12.244
just say "Natty Light."

00:10:12.244 --> 00:10:13.579
And I'm sure Jeanine's
been kicked out

00:10:13.579 --> 00:10:14.680
of her share of Applebee's.

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:15.848
"Alright, Jeanine,
you've had enough."

00:10:15.848 --> 00:10:18.350
"How dare you take away my keys!

00:10:18.350 --> 00:10:21.420
According to the Constitution,
I'm entitled

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:24.723
to as many Long Island iced teas
as I want!"

00:10:24.723 --> 00:10:28.227
And what was so urgent Fox News
felt justified in cutting away

00:10:28.227 --> 00:10:31.063
from the historic impeachment
trial of a former president

00:10:31.063 --> 00:10:32.898
who incited
a violent insurrection?

00:10:32.898 --> 00:10:34.900
What could possibly have been
more important

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:37.069
than the sanctity
of our democracy?

00:10:37.069 --> 00:10:40.505
-"Special Report" is up next
with Bret.

00:10:40.505 --> 00:10:43.808
-Jesse, I'm here, I just can't
seem to get rid of this filter.

00:10:43.808 --> 00:10:46.144
Um, I'm here, though.

00:10:46.144 --> 00:10:49.314
I'm -- I'm not a bear.
[ Laughter ]

00:10:49.314 --> 00:10:51.150
-I have to say,
even in that screen shot,

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:53.185
Jesse Watters still has
the dumber face.

00:10:53.185 --> 00:10:55.820
Leave it to Fox News
to ruin a fun meme.

00:10:55.820 --> 00:10:57.322
Can't we have fun things?

00:10:57.322 --> 00:10:59.992
This is like your dad singing
the lyrics to "WAP."

00:10:59.992 --> 00:11:02.828
But before they could get
to the urgent meme content,

00:11:02.828 --> 00:11:06.165
the five spent time exploding at
each other in an insane argument

00:11:06.165 --> 00:11:09.034
after Juan Williams correctly
accused the rest of the panel

00:11:09.034 --> 00:11:11.203
of ignoring
the impeachment trial.

00:11:11.203 --> 00:11:14.373
-This impeachment trial that
you guys are all ignoring,

00:11:14.373 --> 00:11:17.009
I guess you're afraid of it
because it's a reminder --

00:11:17.009 --> 00:11:18.343
-Don't mind-read, Juan.
Please don't mind-read.

00:11:18.343 --> 00:11:20.012
-Juan, we talked about it
for 10 minutes!

00:11:20.012 --> 00:11:21.680
-Don't mind-read.
-Let me finish! Nah, nah, nah!

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:22.848
-Don't mind-read, then!
-You guys had all the time --

00:11:22.848 --> 00:11:25.183
-Don't read my mind, Juan.
-There's no need!

00:11:25.183 --> 00:11:28.354
-There's no need, 'cause
I listened to all of this!

00:11:28.354 --> 00:11:30.322
So, let me tell you what --
-Then how can you be so wrong?

00:11:30.322 --> 00:11:31.824
-What I heard was --
-How could you be so wrong?

00:11:31.824 --> 00:11:33.992
If you listened,
how can you be so wrong?

00:11:33.992 --> 00:11:35.327
-This trial to me is about

00:11:35.327 --> 00:11:37.362
whether or not Republicans --
-Hey, Juan.

00:11:37.362 --> 00:11:39.698
-...want to close their eyes --
-Hey, Juan. Hold on.

00:11:39.698 --> 00:11:42.200
-Or they want to face the truth.
And right now, let me tell you,

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:44.536
let me tell you,
facing the truth

00:11:44.536 --> 00:11:46.004
is the way that we solve this,

00:11:46.004 --> 00:11:47.506
the way we bring the country
together.

00:11:47.506 --> 00:11:49.841
Ignoring problems is never
the way to solve a problem.

00:11:49.841 --> 00:11:52.177
-You shouldn't be impugning
our intentions, Juan.

00:11:52.177 --> 00:11:53.646
That's the problem.
-That's right.

00:11:53.646 --> 00:11:55.314
-I hope you didn't say we are
standing with these people.

00:11:55.314 --> 00:11:57.082
-I don't need to intuit it.
I can listen.

00:11:57.082 --> 00:11:59.118
I can hear you guys.
-And don't tell me who
to stand with, either.

00:11:59.118 --> 00:12:00.753
-Then it goes into your brain
and it comes out wrong.

00:12:00.753 --> 00:12:02.221
-Ah, that is some
high-Level debate.

00:12:02.221 --> 00:12:05.490
I can't see without my glasses.
Is that Lincoln and Douglas?

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:08.127
"A house divided against itself
cannot stand."

00:12:08.127 --> 00:12:09.294
"That's not what I said,
Lincoln!"

00:12:09.294 --> 00:12:10.796
"Yeah, it is, Douglas."

00:12:10.796 --> 00:12:13.499
"No, it's not! The words are
going into your brain

00:12:13.499 --> 00:12:14.833
and coming out
of your mouth wrong."

00:12:14.833 --> 00:12:17.503
"Oh, yeah? Well, if the words
are coming into my brain,

00:12:17.503 --> 00:12:18.871
they're coming out of your ass!"

00:12:18.871 --> 00:12:20.272
"Well, then I guess that means

00:12:20.272 --> 00:12:21.940
you're eating my ass words,
Douglas."

00:12:21.940 --> 00:12:23.875
"That's not what I said.
Don't read my mind.

00:12:23.875 --> 00:12:25.878
I can feel you reading my mind,
and I don't want you in there.

00:12:25.878 --> 00:12:27.880
Get out of my mind, Lincoln!"

00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:29.447
It's been clear from the start
who Trump was

00:12:29.447 --> 00:12:30.649
and what he stood for.

00:12:30.649 --> 00:12:32.784
Republicans knew it then,
and they know it now.

00:12:32.784 --> 00:12:34.953
They made the same case
Democrats are making now.

00:12:34.953 --> 00:12:36.521
They saw it,
they warned us about it,

00:12:36.521 --> 00:12:37.723
and then they capitulated.

00:12:37.723 --> 00:12:40.059
And that's because they share
Trump's goals.

00:12:40.059 --> 00:12:41.893
They're engaged
in the same project.

00:12:41.893 --> 00:12:43.228
They agree with him.

00:12:43.228 --> 00:12:45.364
They saw that supporting him
was the path to power

00:12:45.364 --> 00:12:47.866
and they jumped on board.
And they're willing to look away

00:12:47.866 --> 00:12:50.769
from any piece of evidence
or tell any lie necessary

00:12:50.769 --> 00:12:53.105
to expunge their guilt,
with one exception.

00:12:53.105 --> 00:12:55.273
There was one instance
yesterday on Fox News

00:12:55.273 --> 00:12:57.643
where someone bravely stood up
and told the truth.

00:12:57.643 --> 00:12:59.645
-I'm not a bear.

00:12:59.645 --> 00:13:01.513
-Thank you.

00:13:01.513 --> 00:13:03.048
This has been "A Closer Look."

